{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004544-vampires-and-photography","id":1004544,"title":"Vampires and Photography","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T11:30:31-08:00","id":1004544,"title":"Vampires and Photography","content":"Right now I'm making a Mekhet that is Photographer and Makes movies. I wanted to know how can he make other kindred show up clearly in his photos ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T11:44:19-08:00","id":1004559,"title":"","content":"Ask them nicely? The effects of the Lost Visage are voluntary, and there's no power in the book that can deny a vampire the ability to use it. You could make a homebrew Devotion or something to do it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:55:11-08:00","id":1004610,"title":"","content":"Are they that voluntary ? I seem to remember that in 1E you could negate it temporarily with a willpower point (or permanently on a given occasion, like for one photograph) with a willpower dot that you had to buy back, but the &quot;Lost Visage&quot; part in 2E doesn't really expand on any of that. I guess given the wording, you could say it's voluntary and can be turned off at will, but that seems pretty much open to interpretation. My impression was more that it was something the beast's presence cause alongside with Vampire's need to lie and hide to survive, and so it was a bit too engraved into kindred existence to be bypassed just like that, but yeah, it's not explicitly said.<br /> <br /> Seems secondary, though. It's not like it's a hugely major point of the setting so you could ask your GM to let you. If your character wants to take pictures without the vampires agreeing to it, then, yeah, I guess a devotion would work, and while I'm not a fan, a Carthian Law would seem thematically appropriate. Carthians could have a Law that lets a few authorized persons break through the lost visage and capture kindred's images. Kind of like they're journalists and they can take pictures of whoever they want (I'd see that as mostly used for blackmail by Carthians). An Invictus oath could be an idea too, the vampire who takes the oath becomes sort of a official portraitist for essentially the same effect.<br /> <br /> Don't really see a Cruac or Theban sorcery ritual for that, seems pretty mundane and silly. A scale could be something, though, a scale developed by a dragon with way too much time on their hands.<br /> <br /> Then, is it the vampire who takes the picture who goes past the lost visage or the camera that's been specially prepared ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:11:27-08:00","id":1004620,"title":"","content":"Since the vampire simply just stands at weird angles instead of appearing as a blur, I don't see why they wouldn't be able to consciously face a camera. Not being able to do so seems like material for a Bane.<br /> <br /> I know that's not how it works, but I always imagine vampires doing this if they stand in front of cameras (starting at 24s):<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UszT_L4QWII?t=24s\" data-code=\"UszT_L4QWII\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UszT_L4QWII/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:25:50-08:00","id":1004627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004544-vampires-and-photography?p=1004610#post1004610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they that voluntary ? I seem to remember that in 1E you could negate it temporarily with a willpower point (or permanently on a given occasion, like for one photograph) with a willpower dot that you had to buy back, but the &amp;quot;Lost Visage&amp;quot; part in 2E doesn't really expand on any of that. I guess given the wording, you could say it's voluntary and can be turned off at will, but that seems pretty much open to interpretation. My impression was more that it was something the beast's presence cause alongside with Vampire's need to lie and hide to survive, and so it was a bit too engraved into kindred existence to be bypassed just like that, but yeah, it's not explicitly said.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly stated in the FAQ. I agree that the book could have done with clearer phrasing on the matter, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004544-vampires-and-photography?p=1004610#post1004610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems secondary, though. It's not like it's a hugely major point of the setting so you could ask your GM to let you. If your character wants to take pictures without the vampires agreeing to it, then, yeah, I guess a devotion would work, and while I'm not a fan, a Carthian Law would seem thematically appropriate. Carthians could have a Law that lets a few authorized persons break through the lost visage and capture kindred's images. Kind of like they're journalists and they can take pictures of whoever they want (I'd see that as mostly used for blackmail by Carthians). An Invictus oath could be an idea too, the vampire who takes the oath becomes sort of a official portraitist for essentially the same effect.<br /> <br /> Don't really see a Cruac or Theban sorcery ritual for that, seems pretty mundane and silly. A scale could be something, though, a scale developed by a dragon with way too much time on their hands.<br /> <br /> Then, is it the vampire who takes the picture who goes past the lost visage or the camera that's been specially prepared ?</div> </div> </div> </div>My version of the Galloi for 2e have a Devotion that lets you anoint someone in blood and (in addition to other effects) make them temporarily gain or lose the benefits of the Lost Visage. I could see a similar Cruac or Theban ritual. Probably low-level ritual and a low target number of successes, since it's a pretty minor effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T03:40:54-08:00","id":1004863,"title":"","content":"Ok, interesting. Guess the setting for my last campaign where vampires made a TV show about a historically accurate story of Longinus didn't even need me to tweak that point. Well, there's still that time where one PC filmed the other three helping each other jump over a street from one building to another (to resolve a hostage situation) an then posted it on youtube and created a meme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T08:18:26-08:00","id":1006717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1004544-vampires-and-photography?p=1004620#post1004620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the vampire simply just stands at weird angles instead of appearing as a blur, I don't see why they wouldn't be able to consciously face a camera. Not being able to do so seems like material for a Bane.<br /> <br /> I know that's not how it works, but I always imagine vampires doing this if they stand in front of cameras (starting at 24s):<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UszT_L4QWII?t=24s\" data-code=\"UszT_L4QWII\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UszT_L4QWII/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my most recent game, one of my players was a Daeva who was a model in life and tried to keep that in his death. He did end up taking that as a bane. he blurred in a photo no matter what. It was pretty awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T22:36:19-08:00","id":1007044,"title":"","content":"Ah I imagined it as the photo comes out just blurred or their beast just some how makes them turn at the just the right time to not show up. Maybe my character could have a relic camera or something that lets him take photos that lets vampires show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]}